cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. CC0 — attribution appreciated, not required."
type: report
title: "The Measure of the Wound: A Sovereign Empirical Record of Black American Structural Distress, 1991–2024"
version: "1.3"
date-released: 2026-09-02
license: CC0-1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/IAMGODIAM/measure-of-the-wound"
url: "https://github.com/IAMGODIAM/measure-of-the-wound"
abstract: >-
  An eight-pillar empirical record of Black American structural disparity across the era of
  formal legal equality, 1991–2024, nested within federal series reaching to 1900 (health),
  1925 (criminal justice), 1940 (housing), 1964 (political participation), 1972 (labor) and
  1514 (historical architecture). Approximately 14,811 raw federal observations synthesized
  into 1,574 verified observations and applied to 15,507 census tracts in 49 cities. Documents
  a consistent pattern: absolute conditions improve while the Black/white ratio holds or widens.
  Publishes its full corrections ledger and an independent verification review as appendices.
keywords:
  - racial inequality
  - wealth gap
  - structural racism
  - Black Americans
  - longitudinal federal data
  - composite index
  - maternal mortality
  - incarceration
  - homeownership
  - open data
